00 + PUT 200 stream reload at 14:56 local, segments resumed 14:56:14) was verified in the prior cycle's session (2026-09-17, relay 0060 work). Known caveats: exterior_5 watchdog events in the same window were NOT attributed to the probe (independent dial-loop history); the 3-wave/7-camera fleet impact numbers come from 09-16 observation. Comment body: --- **Update 2026-09-18 -- both mechanisms confirmed live on master, zero reconnects since the issue was posted, and a wedge-class failure mode** Posting a follow-up after a day of continued observation, all against the same 7-camera frigate 0.17.2 system (go2rtc 1.9.10). **1. Zero reconnects in ~19h with the page closed.** `go2rtc` logs show 0 reconnect lines since this issue was filed (2026-09-17T19:43Z). For comparison, the 3 live-page loads on 09-16 produced 3 fleet-wide reconnect waves (7 sessions remade in the same second, frigate watchdogs restarted all ffmpeg processes ~20-24s later). The trigger really is the live page's per-camera metadata probe (`microphone=` param) and nothing else on our system. **2. The AddTrack path is still undeduped on master.** Re-checked `pkg/rtsp/consumer.go` on master today: `Conn.AddTrack` in the ModeActiveProducer branch still hits `if c.state == StatePlay { c.Reconnect() }` unconditionally, with no check against existing `c.Senders`. Also re-verified that commit fde1fdc5 (recent rtsp refactor) touched `consumer.go` but did not touch this path -- the asymmetry with `Conn.GetTrack`'s pointer-equality receiver dedup (`pkg/rtsp/producer.go`) is unchanged. **3. New: the blast radius is worse than a 20s stall -- consumers can wedge.** A single-probe reproducer (one `GET /api/streams?src=<cam>&video=all&audio=all&microphone=`, no page load) remade the producer's RTSP session as expected. But on the remade session the downstream frigate recorder did not just stall -- it entered a restart loop for ~3 minutes (`No frames received in 20 seconds` x3+, ending in `vf#1 Function not implemented -> Nothing was written`) and never self-healed. It took a go2rtc stream reload (DELETE+PUT on `/api/streams?src=<cam>`) to recover. ...[+6541 chars]
